  "observations": [
    "Queued accounting binds each actual residence success to the single sequential pull, then classifies acceptance or CancellationError at that pull boundary.",
    "Retained eviction and cancellation come from actual residence failed/cancelled endpoints; setup and measured population identities are captured at residence begin.",
    "Waiting direct handoffs require confirmed parked cohorts and publication admission; every pending result is retained and accepted or classified once, including interrupted driver aggregation.",
    "The cleanup loop filters indices below pendingAggregated before awaiting result. Already aggregated owners are neither joined again nor classified again.",
    "Unexpected residence endpoints, overlapping pulls, missing owner evidence, incomplete partitions and non-cancellation errors remain integrity failures even if the driver task is cancelled.",
    "The bounded ledger has a fixed retained-copy ceiling and releases retained identities at terminal endpoints; histograms remain independent.",
    "Native schema 2 rejects schema 1, and scheduler/instrumentation identities change to distinguish the new accounting overhead and incompatible reports.",
    "Cancellation checkpoints execute in benchmark-owned code; the synchronous residence observer neither awaits nor reenters the hub authority.",
    "Runtime regressions preserve the post-await cancellation rejection, actual residence success on dequeue, FIFO and unaffected subscription ownership."
  ],
